      <publication_year>2013</publication_year>
      <description>This line gives the count of plates     
        representing the surface of the numerical shape model of Phoebe,      
        derived from the Implicitly Connected Quadrilateral (ICQ) model with q
        = 128, also included in this data set.  The shape model comprises     
        triangular plates and vertices that are specified in a body-fixed     
        coordinate system.Table of triangular plates of numerical 
        shape model.  These triangular plates approximate the surface of the  
        target.  The corners of each triangular plate are three vertices from 
the vertex table, indicated by vertex number.This line gives the count of vertices   
        representing the surface of the numerical shape model of Phoebe,      
        derived from the Implicitly Connected Quadrilateral (ICQ) model with q
        = 128, also included in this data set.  The shape model comprises     
        triangular plates and vertices that are specified in a body-fixed     
        coordinate system.Table of vertices of numerical shape    
        model. These are the vertices of plates that approximate the surface  
        of the target.  Each row of this table contains the X, Y and Z        
        coordinates of one vertex in a Cartesian coordinate system.</description>
    </Citation_Information>
